792:<section id="gpu-accelerated-exact-and-fuzzy-deduplication">
793:<span id="data-curator-gpu-deduplication"></span><h1>GPU Accelerated Exact and Fuzzy Deduplication<a class="headerlink" href="#gpu-accelerated-exact-and-fuzzy-deduplication" title="Link to this heading">#</a></h1>
796:<p>The exact and fuzzy document-level deduplication modules in NeMo Curator aim to reduce the occurrence of duplicate and
804:<p>As exact deduplication requires significantly less compute, we typically will run exact deduplication before fuzzy deduplication.
805:Also, from our experience in deduplicating Common Crawl snapshots, a significant portion (as high as ~40%) of the duplicates can be exact duplicates.</p>
830:<div class="highlight-python notranslate"><div class="highlight"><pre><span></span><span class="kn">from</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="nn">nemo_curator</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="kn">import</span> <span class="n">ExactDuplicates</span>
834:<span class="n">exact_duplicates</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="n">ExactDuplicates</span><span class="p">(</span>
846:<span class="n">duplicate_docs</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="n">exact_duplicates</span><span class="o">.</span><span class="n">identify_duplicates</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">dataset</span><span class="p">)</span>
858:<span class="n">deduplicated_dataset</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="n">exact_duplicates</span><span class="o">.</span><span class="n">remove</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">dataset</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="n">duplicate_docs</span><span class="p">)</span>
861:<span class="c1"># deduplicated_dataset = exact_duplicates(dataset)</span>
871:<p>Assuming that a unique ID has been added to each document, users can proceed with finding exact duplicates
875:<dt>Find Exact Duplicates</dt><dd><ol class="arabic simple">
877:<li><p>Output: <code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">_exact_duplicates.parquet</span></code>. List of exact duplicates and the document hash.</p></li>
883:<div class="highlight-bash notranslate"><div class="highlight"><pre><span></span><span class="c1"># same as `python nemo_curator/scripts/find_exact_duplicates.py`</span>
902:<section id="fuzzy-deduplication">
903:<h2>Fuzzy Deduplication<a class="headerlink" href="#fuzzy-deduplication" title="Link to this heading">#</a></h2>
904:<p>When removing near-duplicates within the corpus, we perform fuzzy deduplication at the document level in order to remove documents with
905:high Jaccard similarity scores. Our approach closely resembles the approach described in <a class="reference external" href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2201.11990">Smith et al., 2020</a>.</p>
910:<li><p><strong>Compute Minhashes</strong>: The first stage involves computing <a class="reference external" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MinHash">MinHash</a> Signatures on documents.
911:NeMo Curator currently only supports character-based n-grams for MinHashing. An approximate metric of ~4.5 characters per word can be used to determine the n-gram size for users familiar with word-based ngrams.</p></li>
913:to find candidate duplicates.</p></li>
914:<li><p><strong>Buckets to Edgelist</strong>: If not using the false positive check, we directly convert the LSH buckets to edges for the connected components computation.</p></li>
917:<li><p><strong>False Positive Check</strong> <em>(optional alternative to Buckets to Edgelist)</em>: Due to the approximate nature of the bucketing via MinHash + LSH
919:process each of the buckets by computing some pairwise Jaccard similarity scores between documents in each bucket and filter out false positives that might have been hashed into the same bucket.</p></li>
923:<li><p><strong>Jaccard Map Buckets:</strong> Since buckets generated by LSH can have high cardinality, we map multiple LSH buckets to larger batches for
925:for pairwise Jaccard similarity computations within that bucket.</p></li>
926:<li><p><strong>Jaccard Shuffle</strong>: Store documents from the original dataset into new directories and files such that all documents in the same batch (bucket)
927:are stored together. This allows parallelizing pairwise Jaccard similarity computations across different buckets.</p></li>
928:<li><p><strong>Jaccard Compute</strong>: Compute Jaccard similarity scores between all pairs of documents in each bucket to the candidate anchor docs.</p></li>
932:<li><p><strong>Connected Components</strong>: Due to the approximate nature of LSH, documents that are near duplicates may be assigned into different buckets with a few overlapping documents
933:between these buckets. We use a GPU accelerated connected components algorithm to find all connected components in the graph formed by the edges between documents in the same bucket.</p></li>
935:<p>The result from the connected components step is a list of document IDs and the group they belong to.
936:All documents in the same group are considered near duplicates.
937:These results can be used to remove the near duplicates from the corpus.</p>
941:<section id="fuzzydup-pyapi">
942:<span id="id3"></span><h4>Python API<a class="headerlink" href="#fuzzydup-pyapi" title="Link to this heading">#</a></h4>
945:<p>Before running fuzzy deduplication, you need to ensure that the dataset contains a unique ID for each document.
964:<div class="highlight-python notranslate"><div class="highlight"><pre><span></span><span class="kn">from</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="nn">nemo_curator</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="kn">import</span> <span class="n">FuzzyDuplicatesConfig</span>
966:<span class="n">config</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="n">FuzzyDuplicatesConfig</span><span class="p">(</span>
970:    <span class="n">perform_removal</span><span class="o">=</span><span class="kc">False</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="c1"># dictates if deduplicated dataset or IDs of duplicates are returned</span>
997:<div class="highlight-python notranslate"><div class="highlight"><pre><span></span><span class="kn">from</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="nn">nemo_curator</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="kn">import</span> <span class="n">FuzzyDuplicatesConfig</span>
999:<span class="n">config</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="n">FuzzyDuplicatesConfig</span><span class="o">.</span><span class="n">from_yaml</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="s2">&quot;/path/to/config.yaml&quot;</span><span class="p">)</span>
1006:<div class="highlight-python notranslate"><div class="highlight"><pre><span></span><span class="kn">from</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="nn">nemo_curator</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="kn">import</span> <span class="n">FuzzyDuplicates</span>
