1029:<span class="n">deduplicated_dataset</span> <span class="o">=</span> <span class="n">fuzzy_duplicates</span><span class="o">.</span><span class="n">remove</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="n">dataset</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="n">duplicate_docs</span><span class="p">)</span>
1032:<span class="c1"># deduplicated_dataset = fuzzy_duplicates(dataset)</span>
1038:<li><p>A comprehensive example can be found in <a class="reference external" href="https://github.com/NVIDIA/NeMo-Curator/blob/main/examples/fuzzy_deduplication.py">examples/fuzzy_deduplication.py</a>.</p></li>
1039:<li><p>The default values of <code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">num_buckets</span></code> and <code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">hashes_per_bucket</span></code> are set to find documents with an approximately Jaccard similarity of 0.8 or above.</p></li>
1050:<p>Fuzzy deduplication CLI scripts only work with the specific ID format generated by the <code class="code docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">add_id</span></code> script. If the
